509
00:19:36,042 --> 00:19:38,745
If only for the
sake of the others.

510
00:19:38,745 --> 00:19:42,182
- [Crow] I hope to be as
bald as you someday, sir.

511
00:19:42,182 --> 00:19:44,718
- [Tom] Well, we better
sponge out our outfits.

512
00:19:44,718 --> 00:19:47,453
(dramatic music)

513
00:19:49,590 --> 00:19:53,493
- [Mike] I'm gonna say mass
if you wanna hang around.

514
00:19:53,493 --> 00:19:55,028
- [Crow] Well, get over
here and pick out a wig

515
00:19:55,028 --> 00:19:57,097
and let's go trick or treating.

516
00:19:57,097 --> 00:19:59,432
- [Tom] Legends mobile away.

517
00:20:01,302 --> 00:20:03,470
- Listen to me Dobson.

518
00:20:03,470 --> 00:20:06,440
Everything is as planned
for this evening,

519
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:09,710
but there is one
slight alteration.

520
00:20:09,710 --> 00:20:11,778
- [Tom] The party tray
is coming from Subway.

521
00:20:11,778 --> 00:20:14,782
- I shall be at
your house by seven.

522
00:20:14,782 --> 00:20:18,052
- [Tom] Why would you have a
bust of Ron Ealy in your home?

523
00:20:18,052 --> 00:20:20,653
- Dismiss the servants.

524
00:20:20,653 --> 00:20:24,023
I don't want any
strangers interfering.

525
00:20:24,023 --> 00:20:25,725
- [Crow] It's kind
of a noticeable tick.

526
00:20:25,725 --> 00:20:27,893
(gulping)

527
00:20:29,095 --> 00:20:32,265
- [Mike] Parachute/bow tie.

528
00:20:32,265 --> 00:20:34,533
- [Tom] Damn clapper, geez.

529
00:20:36,370 --> 00:20:39,338
- [Crow] David Bernie is the
Aramisman in Wait Until Dark.

530
00:20:39,338 --> 00:20:41,975
(ominous music)

531
00:20:44,177 --> 00:20:46,480
- [Mike] There's cherry
Kool-Aid in my saline bottle.

532
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:49,215
(dramatic music)

533
00:20:50,250 --> 00:20:51,518
- [Tom] Wanna see the pictures?

534
00:20:51,518 --> 00:20:52,987
Your boudoir shots
turned out great.

535
00:20:52,987 --> 00:20:55,722
(dramatic music)

536
00:20:56,890 --> 00:20:58,392
- [Crow] I'm gonna
plunger him senseless.

537
00:20:58,392 --> 00:21:01,395
(dramatic music)

538
00:21:01,395 --> 00:21:03,797
- [Tom] No one interrupts
my prom preparations.

539
00:21:03,797 --> 00:21:06,833
(dramatic music)

540
00:21:06,833 --> 00:21:09,502
- [Crow] Every room in this
hotel comes with an Aztec.

541
00:21:09,502 --> 00:21:11,872
- You see in the dark.

542
00:21:11,872 --> 00:21:13,940
You fall like a cat.

543
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:15,908
You are the Pumaman.

544
00:21:15,908 --> 00:21:17,443
- No, I'm a mad man and
I'll smash your head in

545
00:21:17,443 --> 00:21:19,145
if you take one more step.

546
00:21:19,145 --> 00:21:21,515
- Pumaman does not
kill my people.

547
00:21:21,515 --> 00:21:24,718
- He doesn't, but I
do, now get outta here.

548
00:21:24,718 --> 00:21:28,455
- You can chase me away, but
not the blood in your veins.

549
00:21:28,455 --> 00:21:30,490
Your father saw in the dark.

550
00:21:30,490 --> 00:21:32,225
Your father jumped in the air.

551
00:21:32,225 --> 00:21:34,928
Your father protected my people.

552
00:21:34,928 --> 00:21:36,497
- My father was a physician.

553
00:21:36,497 --> 00:21:39,465
The only he protected
were his patients.

554
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:43,803
- A doctor here, but a great
Pumaman in the Andes plateau.

555
00:21:43,803 --> 00:21:45,372
- [Tom] Oh yeah, he
was for a couple years.

556
00:21:45,372 --> 00:21:47,507
- You're a crazy criminal,
but this is the last time

557
00:21:47,507 --> 00:21:49,843
you go around throwing
people out of windows.

558
00:21:49,843 --> 00:21:51,243
- Before you call the police--

559
00:21:51,243 --> 00:21:52,245
- [Crow] Caress.

560
00:21:52,245 --> 00:21:53,047
- Look.

561
00:21:54,347 --> 00:21:58,318
- [Mike] I'm a representative
of Aztechnologies.

562
00:21:58,318 --> 00:22:02,888
- [Tom] Definitive proof that
he has a copy of that picture.

563
00:22:02,888 --> 00:22:04,892
- [Vadinho] You were
only a boy at the time.

564
00:22:04,892 --> 00:22:07,227
- [Crow] Then you were a girl
and then you were a boy again.

565
00:22:07,227 --> 00:22:09,362
- I did not need to
kill to find you.

566
00:22:09,362 --> 00:22:10,697
- [Mike] I kill for fun.

567
00:22:10,697 --> 00:22:11,932
- Who are you anyway?

568
00:22:11,932 --> 00:22:13,433
- My name is Vadinho.

569
00:22:13,433 --> 00:22:14,667
- [Crow] I'm an onion.

570
00:22:14,667 --> 00:22:16,437
- I'm the high priest
of the temple of the god

571
00:22:16,437 --> 00:22:17,837
who came from other worlds.

572
00:22:17,837 --> 00:22:19,438
- What do you want from me?

573
00:22:19,438 --> 00:22:21,808
- I came to give you this.

574
00:22:21,808 --> 00:22:22,875
- [Tom] Whoa, hey.

575
00:22:22,875 --> 00:22:25,512
- It belonged to your father.

576
00:22:25,512 --> 00:22:29,248
With this, you will have
all the powers he did.

577
00:22:29,248 --> 00:22:30,750
- [Mike] Or your money back.

578
00:22:30,750 --> 00:22:33,320
- I will teach you to use them.

579
00:22:34,788 --> 00:22:35,788
Put it on.

580
00:22:35,788 --> 00:22:36,790
- You're nuts.

581
00:22:36,790 --> 00:22:38,358
- I said put it on.

582
00:22:38,358 --> 00:22:39,893
- The hell with putting it on.

583
00:22:39,893 --> 00:22:41,260
Can you imagine me
showing up at the Dobson's

584
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:42,695
wearing something like that?

585
00:22:42,695 --> 00:22:44,765
- [Crow] Look what you're
wearing now, I mean.

586
00:22:44,765 --> 00:22:46,567
- I say put it on.

587
00:22:46,567 --> 00:22:48,468
- [Mike] And you say put it on.

588
00:22:48,468 --> 00:22:50,203
- And you put it on.

589
00:22:50,203 --> 00:22:52,172
- Okay, pal, okay, take it easy.

590
00:22:52,172 --> 00:22:53,707
- [Tom] I hate it when
Aztecs force themselves

591
00:22:53,707 --> 00:22:55,775
into your hotel room and
make you try on belts.

592
00:22:55,775 --> 00:22:57,677
- [Mike] Nothing worse.

593
00:22:57,677 --> 00:23:00,780
(light clicking)

594
00:23:00,780 --> 00:23:02,982
- [Crow] Wow, look at all
the Farrah Fawcett posters.

595
00:23:02,982 --> 00:23:05,218
(laughing)

596
00:23:06,653 --> 00:23:07,653
- Hey, where's your phone?

597
00:23:07,653 --> 00:23:10,390
I wanna check my
Aztech messages.

598
00:23:11,892 --> 00:23:15,162
(door slamming)

599
00:23:15,162 --> 00:23:17,830
(door creaking)

600
00:23:25,838 --> 00:23:27,040
Come in Nannites.

601
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:28,475
- Hey Spike, what are you doing?

602
00:23:28,475 --> 00:23:30,643
- Oh I gotta get a hair
appointment with the Nannites.

603
00:23:30,643 --> 00:23:32,112
Thinking of getting
that dry look

604
00:23:32,112 --> 00:23:33,580
like the guy in the Puma movie.

605
00:23:33,580 --> 00:23:35,748
- Mike, your sense of style,
as always, is unerring.

606
00:23:35,748 --> 00:23:37,150
Go for it, you turkey.

607
00:23:37,150 --> 00:23:38,618
- Hi, can I help you?

608
00:23:38,618 --> 00:23:41,455
- Oh well yeah, I had a
hair appointment for now.

609
00:23:41,455 --> 00:23:42,722
- Oh hi Mike.

610
00:23:42,722 --> 00:23:45,558
Are we gonna do the
same as last time or?

611
00:23:45,558 --> 00:23:47,693
- Ooh, well hi Shelly.

612
00:23:47,693 --> 00:23:52,232
No offense, but last time you
made my hair 70 miles high.

613
00:23:52,232 --> 00:23:53,933
So I was wondering if
any of the other stylists

614
00:23:53,933 --> 00:23:56,402
were available,
Decka or Shondelle.

615
00:23:56,402 --> 00:23:58,538
- Oh, I see, I understand.

616
00:24:00,173 --> 00:24:01,808
- Great 'cause I don't mean to--

617
00:24:01,808 --> 00:24:04,043
- They're all busy, I just
checked, it's just me.

618
00:24:04,043 --> 00:24:06,445
Now what do you want?

619
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:10,283
- Well, if I could
get the dry look,

620
00:24:10,283 --> 00:24:11,618
if it's not too much trouble.

621
00:24:11,618 --> 00:24:13,453
- Trouble, why would
it be any trouble?

622
00:24:13,453 --> 00:24:14,888
It's no trouble at all.

623
00:24:14,888 --> 00:24:18,558
So, you got the day off today,
or you live around here,

624
00:24:18,558 --> 00:24:20,927
or is it pretty nice out today?

625
00:24:20,927 --> 00:24:23,697
There, you're
done, the dry look.

626
00:24:24,563 --> 00:24:26,098
- Well, thanks Shelly.

627
00:24:26,098 --> 00:24:27,833
I hope I didn't offend you.

628
00:24:27,833 --> 00:24:30,070
Ooh, so sensitive, man.

629
00:24:30,070 --> 00:24:33,138
- Mike, I think she might've
went just a little too dry.

630
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:34,173
- What are you talking about?

631
00:24:34,173 --> 00:24:35,875
I'm sure it's, ow, ooh.

632
00:24:35,875 --> 00:24:37,843
Well, maybe she went a
little heavy on the mousse,

633
00:24:37,843 --> 00:24:40,480
but once I shower I'm
sure it'll be fine.

634
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:41,948
We'll be right back.

635
00:24:41,948 --> 00:24:43,750
- If we can just redirect
a river onto your head

636
00:24:43,750 --> 00:24:44,817
I think we can salvage it.

637
00:24:44,817 --> 00:24:45,818
- So you like it?

638
00:24:45,818 --> 00:24:47,187
- No.

639
00:24:47,187 --> 00:24:49,755
(upbeat music)

640
00:24:53,793 --> 00:24:57,697
- Father, I'd like to introduce
you to Professor Farms,

641
00:24:57,697 --> 00:25:00,000
the paleontologist I spoke
so much to you about.

642
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:01,200
- Welcome Professor.

643
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,202
- Thank you.

644
00:25:02,202 --> 00:25:03,403
- [Tom] These are some old guys.

645
00:25:03,403 --> 00:25:05,972
- Sir George Bradley
of the Energy Ministry,

646
00:25:05,972 --> 00:25:09,808
Sir John Forbes Esquith,
Sir Michael Robinson.

647
00:25:10,710 --> 00:25:11,845
- [Mike] Minister of Waffles.

648
00:25:11,845 --> 00:25:13,680
(dramatic music)

649
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:14,680
- [Crow] Where's the keg?

650
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:17,883
(dramatic music)

651
00:25:17,883 --> 00:25:21,688
- [Mike] We're here to
pick up our Grammys.

652
00:25:21,688 --> 00:25:24,623
- [Tom] (clears throat) I'm
afraid I ran over your dog

653
00:25:24,623 --> 00:25:27,093
in the driveway, I'm sorry.

654
00:25:27,093 --> 00:25:29,828
(dramatic music)

655
00:25:31,197 --> 00:25:34,733
- [Mike] My name is
Pleasence and I am funky.

656
00:25:36,837 --> 00:25:38,070
- [Tom] It's better
than when he wore

657
00:25:38,070 --> 00:25:40,373
his little black
dress, I suppose.

658
00:25:40,373 --> 00:25:42,242
- [Mike] Battle of
the network eye bags.

659
00:25:42,242 --> 00:25:45,345
(dramatic music)

660
00:25:45,345 --> 00:25:49,315
- [Crow] Oh no, they're
gonna start tangoing.

661
00:25:49,315 --> 00:25:52,352
- [Tom] I'm sorry, this is a
no English has beens party.

662
00:25:52,352 --> 00:25:54,787
(dramatic music)

663
00:25:54,787 --> 00:25:56,155
- [Mike] What kind of
party clown are you?

664
00:25:56,155 --> 00:25:58,157
I'm not paying for this.

665
00:25:59,792 --> 00:26:03,162
- [Crow] Hip Donald
room clearer Pleasence.

666
00:26:03,162 --> 00:26:04,932
- [Tom] It's my irritable
bowel syndrome isn't it?

667
00:26:04,932 --> 00:26:07,667
(dramatic music)

668
00:26:10,603 --> 00:26:12,405
- [Mike] With Mitchum,
I can skip a day.

669
00:26:12,405 --> 00:26:14,740
- [Crow] Sugar frosted eyes.

670
00:26:14,740 --> 00:26:18,043
(dramatic music)

671
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:22,048
- [Tom] I was supposed to
bring an appetizer wasn't I?

672
00:26:22,048 --> 00:26:25,518
- [Mike] Well,
who's for foosball?

673
00:26:25,518 --> 00:26:28,855
- Another one of my father's
very important friends.

674
00:26:28,855 --> 00:26:30,123
- [Crow] Oh I thought
it was your aunt.

675
00:26:30,123 --> 00:26:33,560
(dramatic music)

676
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:34,560
- What's the matter?

677
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,795
- [Tom] I'm bored.

678
00:26:35,795 --> 00:26:37,630
- I don't know.

679
00:26:37,630 --> 00:26:40,267
I get this way when I
sense some sort of danger.

680
00:26:40,267 --> 00:26:41,968
- [Mike] Or some
sort of breasts.

681
00:26:41,968 --> 00:26:44,570
- With me, what
could be dangerous?

682
00:26:44,570 --> 00:26:45,872
- [Crow] Wearing
loose fitting clothing

683
00:26:45,872 --> 00:26:47,607
around a power takeoff
could be dangerous.

684
00:26:47,607 --> 00:26:49,342
- Your charm perhaps.

685
00:26:50,510 --> 00:26:52,978
- (laughs) You're not
doing so badly yourself

686
00:26:52,978 --> 00:26:54,580
for a paleontologist.

687
00:26:54,580 --> 00:26:56,548
- Well, I'm from the
neanderthal school,

688
00:26:56,548 --> 00:26:59,652
and occasionally my
primitive instincts pop up.

689
00:26:59,652 --> 00:27:01,988
- [Tom] Wanna go and
circle a mammoth later?

690
00:27:01,988 --> 00:27:05,258
- You're sounding
much better Professor.

691
00:27:05,258 --> 00:27:07,227
- You make me feel like
I'm still in the museum.

692
00:27:07,227 --> 00:27:09,062
Why don't you just call me Tony?

693
00:27:09,062 --> 00:27:10,163
- Okay, Tony.

694
00:27:12,165 --> 00:27:14,333
- [Mike] Let me show
you the way out.

695
00:27:14,333 --> 00:27:16,235
Please don't come back.

696
00:27:17,437 --> 00:27:20,307
- This is where I
keep all my books.

697
00:27:21,775 --> 00:27:25,512
So, dinosaurs became extinct
because they no longer knew

698
00:27:25,512 --> 00:27:26,913
how to love each other.

699
00:27:26,913 --> 00:27:28,280
Is that correct?

700
00:27:28,280 --> 00:27:29,915
- [Tom] In a wrong
kinda way, sure.

701
00:27:29,915 --> 00:27:32,218
- Exactly, and I certainly
wouldn't want our species

702
00:27:32,218 --> 00:27:33,920
to end the same way.

703
00:27:33,920 --> 00:27:35,455
- [Crow] All aboard.

704
00:27:35,455 --> 00:27:39,425
- That's the best biological
blackmail I've ever heard.

705
00:27:39,425 --> 00:27:42,762
- [Tom] But Mike, this
is called kissing.

706
00:27:42,762 --> 00:27:45,032
Maybe you can try this
with someone someday.

707
00:27:45,032 --> 00:27:46,867
- [Mike] Well thanks, hey.

708
00:27:46,867 --> 00:27:49,468
(Tom giggling)

709
00:27:52,372 --> 00:27:53,573
I hate your crotch.

710
00:27:53,573 --> 00:27:54,407
(hands slapping)

711
00:27:54,407 --> 00:27:56,642
(groaning)

712
00:27:59,445 --> 00:28:01,180
- [Tom] All right,
disco fighting.

713
00:28:01,180 --> 00:28:03,917
(hands slapping)

714
00:28:05,518 --> 00:28:07,453
- [Crow] He's totally
pounding Eddy Raddich.

715
00:28:07,453 --> 00:28:08,622
- [Mike] Whoa.

716
00:28:10,423 --> 00:28:11,858
Man, the Dutch
embassy's neighbors

717
00:28:11,858 --> 00:28:13,192
must always be calling the cops.

718
00:28:13,192 --> 00:28:15,262
(groaning)

719
00:28:15,262 --> 00:28:18,030
(hands slapping)

720
00:28:19,498 --> 00:28:23,903
- [Crow] Tiny halls for the
narrow shouldered among us.

721
00:28:25,105 --> 00:28:27,540
- [Tom] Great, we're
late for tap class.

722
00:28:28,975 --> 00:28:33,145
- [Mike] Ironic, he looks
like a waiter and he's dumb.

723
00:28:35,013 --> 00:28:37,517
- [Crow] Al Pacino's elevator.

724
00:28:39,652 --> 00:28:41,187
- [Tom] Apparently,
the house capsized

725
00:28:41,187 --> 00:28:42,355
and he and Shelly Winters

726
00:28:42,355 --> 00:28:45,525
have to climb up
through the basement.

727
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:50,563
- [Mike] Man, I gotta get
that order out to table six.

728
00:28:50,563 --> 00:28:53,967
Why is the kitchen so
far from the dining room?

729
00:28:53,967 --> 00:28:58,638
- [Crow] He's in a attic,
attic, attica, attica, attica.

730
00:29:00,140 --> 00:29:04,110
- [Tom] He's gonna write
Pumaman rules on the wall.

731
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:08,782
(wood crashing)

732
00:29:08,782 --> 00:29:10,015
- [Mike] Thank goodness
they made their house

733
00:29:10,015 --> 00:29:12,018
out of peanut brittle.

734
00:29:12,018 --> 00:29:16,422
- [Crow] So basically, a mild
rain could take out that roof.

735
00:29:16,422 --> 00:29:20,260
- [Tom] My favorite
ball, I will not lose it.

736
00:29:20,260 --> 00:29:23,395
- [Mike] Man, there's a lot
of reindeer crap up here.

737
00:29:23,395 --> 00:29:26,432
(dramatic music)

738
00:29:26,432 --> 00:29:29,402
- [Crow] Like an
idiot on the roof.

739
00:29:29,402 --> 00:29:31,905
(Tom meowing)

740
00:29:33,773 --> 00:29:38,678
- [Mike] Spends next three
hours running from edge to edge.

741
00:29:40,647 --> 00:29:42,115
- Tony!

742
00:29:42,115 --> 00:29:46,518
- [Crow] It's Gino, I've been
looking for you, you Mook.

743
00:29:49,188 --> 00:29:53,292
- [Mike] Here, here's
a garter snake for you.

744
00:29:53,292 --> 00:29:57,297
- [Crow] The world's most
persistent belt salesman.

745
00:29:57,297 --> 00:30:01,267
- [Tom] There, lower
yourself down with that.

746
00:30:01,267 --> 00:30:02,268
- Put it on!

747
00:30:02,268 --> 00:30:03,102
- Then what?

748
00:30:03,102 --> 00:30:03,937
- Jump!

749
00:30:03,937 --> 00:30:04,803
- I'll be killed.

750
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:05,905
- Put it on!

751
00:30:05,905 --> 00:30:06,907
- [Crow] And then get killed.

752
00:30:06,907 --> 00:30:10,142
(dramatic music)

753
00:30:10,142 --> 00:30:11,543
- [Mike] You know what, my
mom had a pair of earrings

754
00:30:11,543 --> 00:30:13,613
that did the exact same thing.

755
