gods are coming from space

1003
00:40:35,935 --> 00:40:38,570
to tell you you must serve
or evil will triumphant.

1004
00:40:38,570 --> 00:40:41,840
- Oh wow, well I see a
beach ball and a string,

1005
00:40:41,840 --> 00:40:43,008
and a string and a pulley.

1006
00:40:43,008 --> 00:40:44,343
There's Gypsy, hey Gypsy.

1007
00:40:44,343 --> 00:40:45,343
- [Gypsy] Hey Mike, sorry.

1008
00:40:45,343 --> 00:40:46,645
- That's all right.

1009
00:40:46,645 --> 00:40:48,247
- She's doing the
will of the gods.

1010
00:40:48,247 --> 00:40:49,548
- Just pay no attention to her.

1011
00:40:49,548 --> 00:40:51,183
- Well you know what, hey Gyps,

1012
00:40:51,183 --> 00:40:52,918
I really am gonna
grab those noodles.

1013
00:40:52,918 --> 00:40:53,918
You wanna split them with me?

1014
00:40:53,918 --> 00:40:54,987
- [Gypsy] Yay, yummy, let's go.

1015
00:40:54,987 --> 00:40:56,088
- Okay, let's go.

1016
00:40:56,088 --> 00:40:57,388
- There goes our God.

1017
00:40:57,388 --> 00:41:01,060
- Well, it would appear
that he is not yet ready

1018
00:41:01,060 --> 00:41:03,128
to accept his Coatimundi nature.

1019
00:41:03,128 --> 00:41:07,967
- Yes, and the gods are
certainly, and the gods will be.

1020
00:41:07,967 --> 00:41:09,902
Man, they're gonna finish
all the cold sesame noodles.

1021
00:41:09,902 --> 00:41:11,337
(alarm buzzing)
- Let's go, let's go.

1022
00:41:11,337 --> 00:41:12,505
Yeah, that's his movie sign.

1023
00:41:12,505 --> 00:41:13,338
- We're not gonna get any.

1024
00:41:13,338 --> 00:41:14,607
(alarm buzzing)

1025
00:41:14,607 --> 00:41:17,643
(door slamming)

1026
00:41:17,643 --> 00:41:20,245
(water dripping)

1027
00:41:20,245 --> 00:41:22,915
(door creaking)

1028
00:41:26,018 --> 00:41:27,720
You ate all the sesame
noodles, didn't you?

1029
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:29,355
- [Mike] Yeah, they're all gone.

1030
00:41:29,355 --> 00:41:30,788
(dramatic music)

1031
00:41:30,788 --> 00:41:31,990
- Help me, father.

1032
00:41:31,990 --> 00:41:32,858
- [Crow] My homework
is really hard.

1033
00:41:32,858 --> 00:41:36,395
(dramatic music)

1034
00:41:36,395 --> 00:41:37,530
- [Mike] Excuse
me, coming through.

1035
00:41:37,530 --> 00:41:40,065
(dramatic music)

1036
00:41:40,065 --> 00:41:41,400
- [Crow] Bold, Mike.

1037
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:42,233
- [Mike] Thanks.

1038
00:41:42,233 --> 00:41:43,502
- Help me, father.

1039
00:41:43,502 --> 00:41:45,670
- [Tom] I need a couple
of bucks to make rent.

1040
00:41:45,670 --> 00:41:46,672
- Help me Vadinho.

1041
00:41:46,672 --> 00:41:48,273
♪ Help me Vadinho ♪

1042
00:41:48,273 --> 00:41:49,508
♪ Help, help me Vadinho ♪

1043
00:41:49,508 --> 00:41:52,243
(dramatic music)

1044
00:41:53,945 --> 00:41:55,480
- [Tom] (sniffs) They have cats.

1045
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:57,148
Oh no, that's me.

1046
00:41:57,148 --> 00:41:59,150
Would you take that off?

1047
00:41:59,150 --> 00:42:00,852
- [Crow] Look, just don't
use the holodeck anymore,

1048
00:42:00,852 --> 00:42:02,387
if you don't know how to use it.

1049
00:42:02,387 --> 00:42:05,290
- (exhales) Thank you.

1050
00:42:05,290 --> 00:42:07,325
- [Mike] Guy who lives
on the second floor.

1051
00:42:07,325 --> 00:42:09,828
- [Tom] You're pretty.

1052
00:42:09,828 --> 00:42:11,130
- Did you find it?

1053
00:42:11,130 --> 00:42:11,963
- No.

1054
00:42:13,432 --> 00:42:14,633
- [Crow] Then what
are you doing?

1055
00:42:14,633 --> 00:42:16,068
I thought you were
gonna find it.

1056
00:42:16,068 --> 00:42:17,368
I mean, it's okay, I just
thought you were gonna find it.

1057
00:42:17,368 --> 00:42:18,837
- But I learned that I
can only project myself

1058
00:42:18,837 --> 00:42:20,838
to a place that I know.

1059
00:42:20,838 --> 00:42:22,842
I have to know exactly
where I wanna go,

1060
00:42:22,842 --> 00:42:25,710
otherwise I'll get lost
in the nothingness.

1061
00:42:25,710 --> 00:42:27,012
- [Mike] So it's off to Hooters.

1062
00:42:27,012 --> 00:42:28,180
- Then we are no closer.

1063
00:42:28,180 --> 00:42:29,213
- [Tom] So you whizzed it?

1064
00:42:29,213 --> 00:42:30,615
- Listen Vadinho--

1065
00:42:30,615 --> 00:42:33,018
- [Crow] Are you
a kind of onion?

1066
00:42:33,018 --> 00:42:35,653
- Is finding the
mask the only way?

1067
00:42:35,653 --> 00:42:40,492
- Yes, if you do not succeed,
terrible things will happen.

1068
00:42:40,492 --> 00:42:42,628
- [Tom] The gods will
give you the wet look.

1069
00:42:42,628 --> 00:42:44,195
- They have lost
their connection.

1070
00:42:44,195 --> 00:42:45,932
- [Mike] The network is down.

1071
00:42:45,932 --> 00:42:48,200
- The mask is serving evil.

1072
00:42:48,200 --> 00:42:50,902
- Can't they do
anything from up there?

1073
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:53,838
- Man is free, man
is master of himself.

1074
00:42:53,838 --> 00:42:55,207
- [Crow] Man sounds cool.

1075
00:42:55,207 --> 00:42:58,110
- But if they come,
man is no longer free.

1076
00:42:58,110 --> 00:42:59,812
- [Tom] And it could get pricey.

1077
00:42:59,812 --> 00:43:01,980
- You must concentrate.

1078
00:43:01,980 --> 00:43:04,215
You will find the
solution in your mind.

1079
00:43:04,215 --> 00:43:05,917
- [Mike] I think we saw
the limits of his mind

1080
00:43:05,917 --> 00:43:07,787
just a few minutes ago.

1081
00:43:09,053 --> 00:43:12,892
- [Crow] Let's not be
roommates anymore, okay?

1082
00:43:14,092 --> 00:43:15,893
- [Tom] I'm thinking of
having my chin smaller.

1083
00:43:15,893 --> 00:43:18,497
(upbeat music)

1084
00:43:19,765 --> 00:43:23,368
I'm in the fire truck
for USA up all night.

1085
00:43:24,803 --> 00:43:26,505
- [Crow] Soundtrack by my
little brother's Casio.

1086
00:43:26,505 --> 00:43:29,073
(upbeat music)

1087
00:43:30,508 --> 00:43:32,812
- [Tom] I keep dreaming of
a little man in a tiny car.

1088
00:43:32,812 --> 00:43:34,547
- [Mike] Hi.

1089
00:43:34,547 --> 00:43:36,915
- Where did you come from?

1090
00:43:36,915 --> 00:43:38,050
- Out there.

1091
00:43:38,050 --> 00:43:40,118
- What sort of story is that?

1092
00:43:40,118 --> 00:43:41,020
- I'm the Pumaman.

1093
00:43:41,020 --> 00:43:41,820
- [Mike] Wait, who is this Guy?

1094
00:43:41,820 --> 00:43:42,755
- Who is he?

1095
00:43:42,755 --> 00:43:43,555
Somebody out of a comic strip?

1096
00:43:43,555 --> 00:43:44,690
I've never heard of him.

1097
00:43:44,690 --> 00:43:46,492
- He didn't materialize
until yesterday.

1098
00:43:46,492 --> 00:43:47,760
- Well are you getting
anything out of it?

1099
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:49,193
- Mostly trouble.

1100
00:43:49,193 --> 00:43:51,130
- I told you Tony, if
you want adventure,

1101
00:43:51,130 --> 00:43:52,630
why don't you join up with us?

1102
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:54,533
It's all the sports you can
take, high jump, low jump.

1103
00:43:54,533 --> 00:43:56,135
You get a free sword
at the end of it.

1104
00:43:56,135 --> 00:43:57,703
- I'll keep that
in mind, Martin.

1105
00:43:57,703 --> 00:43:59,738
But in the meantime, you
wouldn't happen to have

1106
00:43:59,738 --> 00:44:01,640
a transmitter and receiver
to lend me, would you?

1107
00:44:01,640 --> 00:44:03,308
- You mean a position indicator.

1108
00:44:03,308 --> 00:44:06,345
- [Crow] Hey, an
old donut back here.

1109
00:44:06,345 --> 00:44:07,578
- [Tom] Here's your pacemaker.

1110
00:44:07,578 --> 00:44:09,047
Thanks for letting me borrow it.

1111
00:44:09,047 --> 00:44:12,250
(transmitter beeping)

1112
00:44:12,250 --> 00:44:13,718
- How does it work?

1113
00:44:13,718 --> 00:44:15,987
- The closer you get, the
more constant the bleep.

1114
00:44:15,987 --> 00:44:17,255
- Over what range?

1115
00:44:17,255 --> 00:44:18,757
- Up to two miles.

1116
00:44:19,958 --> 00:44:22,027
- Okay, if you slow
down, I'll get out.

1117
00:44:22,027 --> 00:44:23,128
- We're here?

1118
00:44:23,128 --> 00:44:24,830
- No, I'm going the other way.

1119
00:44:24,830 --> 00:44:27,432
- What did you say you
do, the sandwich man?

1120
00:44:27,432 --> 00:44:29,067
- No, the Pumaman.

1121
00:44:29,067 --> 00:44:31,337
That's a whole different bag.

1122
00:44:31,337 --> 00:44:32,470
- What are you advertising?

1123
00:44:32,470 --> 00:44:33,905
- Men from outer space.

1124
00:44:33,905 --> 00:44:35,673
- [Tom] He is the Pumaman.

1125
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:40,412
He can get out of a car
going three miles an hour.

1126
00:44:40,412 --> 00:44:41,913
Wow, the queen.

1127
00:44:41,913 --> 00:44:43,015
(tires squealing)

1128
00:44:43,015 --> 00:44:45,583
(car crashing)

1129
00:44:45,583 --> 00:44:46,818
- [Crow] That steering column

1130
00:44:46,818 --> 00:44:48,487
plunged through his
chest, that's great.

1131
00:44:48,487 --> 00:44:50,588
- [Tom] Lost control of
me bladder, sorry mates.

1132
00:44:50,588 --> 00:44:53,225
(water spraying)

1133
00:44:53,225 --> 00:44:54,660
- [Mike] Do you have
the jaws of life on you?

1134
00:44:54,660 --> 00:44:55,860
(water spraying)

1135
00:44:55,860 --> 00:44:57,328
(laughing)

1136
00:44:57,328 --> 00:44:58,763
- [Crow] I have a good mind
to join a marching band.

1137
00:44:58,763 --> 00:45:00,865
(laughs)

1138
00:45:01,800 --> 00:45:03,302
(water spraying)

1139
00:45:03,302 --> 00:45:06,238
- [Mike] Where am I gonna get
another personal fire truck?

1140
00:45:06,238 --> 00:45:09,007
(water spraying)

1141
00:45:11,177 --> 00:45:13,912
(dramatic music)

1142
00:45:15,413 --> 00:45:20,018
- [Tom] Oh I did deserve all
those beatings as a child.

1143
00:45:21,487 --> 00:45:22,320
(beeping)

1144
00:45:22,320 --> 00:45:23,622
- [Mike] Cupid.

1145
00:45:23,622 --> 00:45:26,358
(dramatic music)

1146
00:45:28,193 --> 00:45:29,127
- Here he comes.

1147
00:45:29,127 --> 00:45:31,263
- [Crow] Light the candles.

1148
00:45:32,663 --> 00:45:35,667
- [Tom] Just trying to net some
tuna and we got this thing.

1149
00:45:35,667 --> 00:45:36,902
- Call him.

1150
00:45:36,902 --> 00:45:38,437
- [Mike] He was playing
with mommy's lipstick.

1151
00:45:38,437 --> 00:45:41,907
(dramatic music)

1152
00:45:41,907 --> 00:45:44,275
- Don't come in Tony, run!

1153
00:45:44,275 --> 00:45:45,910
- [Crow] Eat this
baguette, eat it!

1154
00:45:45,910 --> 00:45:46,778
(yelling)

1155
00:45:46,778 --> 00:45:47,712
Grrr, grrr.

1156
00:45:50,815 --> 00:45:52,717
- [Mike] Stuck him in.

1157
00:45:52,717 --> 00:45:55,320
(groaning)

1158
00:45:55,320 --> 00:45:58,457
(dramatic music)

1159
00:45:58,457 --> 00:45:59,825
- [Crow] More ketchup, please.

1160
00:45:59,825 --> 00:46:02,760
- Don't worry about
me, watch out!

1161
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:04,028
- [Tom] He has this
trolling motor on them.

1162
00:46:04,028 --> 00:46:06,498
(dramatic music)

1163
00:46:06,498 --> 00:46:08,567
- [Crow] Ooh, I think he
officially bonked them.

1164
00:46:08,567 --> 00:46:11,303
(dramatic music)

1165
00:46:12,703 --> 00:46:16,808
- [Tom] Beat me, fine,
but to drape a net on me.

1166
00:46:16,808 --> 00:46:18,210
- [Mike] And then
they snagged on me,

1167
00:46:18,210 --> 00:46:19,410
and called me Prince Valiant,

1168
00:46:19,410 --> 00:46:22,647
and said I had a
stupid fakey religion.

1169
00:46:23,982 --> 00:46:25,817
(tires squealing)

1170
00:46:25,817 --> 00:46:28,253
- [Tom] Don't let them net me.

1171
00:46:28,253 --> 00:46:29,955
- Save yourself.

1172
00:46:29,955 --> 00:46:30,788
(tires squealing)

1173
00:46:30,788 --> 00:46:33,558
Disappear, please do it.

1174
00:46:33,558 --> 00:46:35,327
(dramatic music)

1175
00:46:35,327 --> 00:46:36,862
- [Crow] Do the hustle.

1176
00:46:36,862 --> 00:46:38,963
- [Tom] Score, it's good.

1177
00:46:40,465 --> 00:46:42,067
- [Crow] Into this
piece of drywall.

1178
00:46:42,067 --> 00:46:44,670
(upbeat music)

1179
00:46:49,173 --> 00:46:51,510
- [Mike] He's just
doing his floor routine.

1180
00:46:51,510 --> 00:46:52,510
- [Man] There he is!

1181
00:46:52,510 --> 00:46:53,978
(gun firing)

1182
00:46:53,978 --> 00:46:56,147
- [Crow] Ow, ow, ow,
I'm dead, okay, ow, ow.

1183
00:46:56,147 --> 00:46:58,183
(gun firing)

1184
00:46:58,183 --> 00:46:59,250
- [Tom] The molasses.

1185
00:46:59,250 --> 00:47:00,152
- [Man] I don't see him anymore!

1186
00:47:00,152 --> 00:47:01,253
- [Man] Keep shooting anyway!

1187
00:47:01,253 --> 00:47:02,955
(gun firing)

1188
00:47:02,955 --> 00:47:04,322
- [Crow] I don't even think
he knows these guys are here.

1189
00:47:04,322 --> 00:47:05,323
He's just playing around.

1190
00:47:05,323 --> 00:47:07,125
(gun firing)

1191
00:47:07,125 --> 00:47:08,260
- [Tom] Weee, this is fun.

1192
00:47:08,260 --> 00:47:10,695
(gun firing)

1193
00:47:10,695 --> 00:47:11,897
- [Mike] I love the Pumaman.

1194
00:47:11,897 --> 00:47:13,498
(gun firing)

1195
00:47:13,498 --> 00:47:15,033
- [Man] (yells) Shoot!

1196
00:47:15,033 --> 00:47:16,602
- [Crow] And 10 to 12 hours,
they should be out of ammo.

1197
00:47:16,602 --> 00:47:19,203
(gun firing)

1198
00:47:19,203 --> 00:47:20,205
- [Tom] My cape hock.

1199
00:47:20,205 --> 00:47:22,640
(gun firing)

1200
00:47:24,977 --> 00:47:26,478
- [Mike] Just wanna
check your axle here.

1201
00:47:26,478 --> 00:47:28,713
(man yelling)

1202
00:47:28,713 --> 00:47:30,415
- [Man] Brakes, step on
the brakes, do something!

1203
00:47:30,415 --> 00:47:32,417
(man yelling)

1204
00:47:32,417 --> 00:47:33,452
- [Crow] Oh, so this lousy movie

1205
00:47:33,452 --> 00:47:34,753
ruins a perfect good Jaguar.

1206
00:47:34,753 --> 00:47:36,955
(gun firing)

1207
00:47:36,955 --> 00:47:38,023
- [Mike] Hi, what's going on?

1208
00:47:38,023 --> 00:47:40,392
(upbeat music)

1209
00:47:40,392 --> 00:47:42,160
- [Tom] The archangels wane.

1210
00:47:42,160 --> 00:47:43,395
(groaning)

1211
00:47:43,395 --> 00:47:47,265
- Tony, you have
power in your hands.

1212
00:47:47,265 --> 00:47:49,333
Your hands are claws.

1213
00:47:49,333 --> 00:47:51,102
- [Mike] Sorry, I forgot
to tell you about that.

1214
00:47:51,102 --> 00:47:54,338
- [Crow] Pumaman can rip
through pure contact paper.

1215
00:47:54,338 --> 00:47:56,140
(men yelling)

1216
00:47:56,140 --> 00:47:57,642
- [Man] Shoot him!

1217
00:47:58,710 --> 00:48:00,978
- [Mike] I am
joining your carpool.

1218
00:48:00,978 --> 00:48:03,582
- [Tom] These poor guys
aren't even the villains.

1219
00:48:03,582 --> 00:48:07,018
They just came to get some
stuff out of their You-Store-It.

1220
00:48:07,018 --> 00:48:12,023
- [Crow] Well, time to drop in
on the Superbowl at halftime.

1221
00:48:13,158 --> 00:48:15,493
- [Mike] Meanwhile,
in Georgie Girl.

1222
00:48:15,493 --> 00:48:19,632
- [Tom] Oh, she's driving
the camera man to school.

1223
00:48:19,632 --> 00:48:20,965
- [Crow] Snoopy.

1224
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:23,502
(beeping)

1225
00:48:23,502 --> 00:48:25,637
- [Mike] Now he just pops
into old girlfriend's cars.

1226
00:48:25,637 --> 00:48:26,605
- Tony, how'd you get here?

1227
00:48:26,605 --> 00:48:27,605
- Nevermind, drive.

1228
00:48:27,605 --> 00:48:28,807
- [Tom] He said.

1229
00:48:28,807 --> 00:48:30,308
- But they'll kill
you if they find you.

1230
00:48:30,308 --> 00:48:32,843
Kobras wants to kill you
and they're following me.

1231
00:48:32,843 --> 00:48:34,078
They're right behind me.

1232
00:48:34,078 --> 00:48:35,547
- Nevermind, tell me
where the mask is.

1233
00:48:35,547 --> 00:48:36,882
- [Crow] Get your
copy at Blockbuster.

1234
00:48:36,882 --> 00:48:39,317
- Don't ask me that, I can't.

1235
00:48:39,317 --> 00:48:42,253
I swear I'd like
to, but I can't.

1236
00:48:42,253 --> 00:48:45,157
On condition to keep the
secret, just like everyone,

1237
00:48:45,157 --> 00:48:46,858
I can't do it.

1238
00:48:46,858 --> 00:48:49,293
- Try, fight him, fight
him with your will.

1239
00:48:49,293 --> 00:48:50,728
- [Mike] But my will won't.

1240
00:48:50,728 --> 00:48:53,665
- I can't, he's commanding
me from a distance.

1241
00:48:53,665 --> 00:48:54,833
- [Tom] Amelia Airhead.

1242
00:48:54,833 --> 00:48:56,167
- I can't do it.

1243
00:48:56,167 --> 00:48:58,103
Tony, help me, free me.

1244
00:49:00,238 --> 00:49:03,875
Something terrible's happening
to me and to everyone.

1245
00:49:03,875 --> 00:49:06,210
Help me, don't leave me.

1246
00:49:06,210 --> 00:49:09,247
- [Crow] Is that
a helmet or a hat?

1247
00:49:09,247 --> 00:49:12,083
- [Mike] Sorry, we
stopped for slurpees.

1248
00:49:12,083 --> 00:49:13,252
- There they are, run.

1249
00:49:13,252 --> 00:49:14,820
Run, save yourself.

1250
00:49:15,987 --> 00:49:18,123
- [Crow] Play your theme
