- Your body no longer
belongs to you.

1490
01:00:38,703 --> 01:00:42,740
The forces of the cosmo
have turned you over to me.

1491
01:00:42,740 --> 01:00:43,942
- [Tom] Are the heads
eating potato chips?

1492
01:00:43,942 --> 01:00:45,410
- Come back to me!

1493
01:00:46,343 --> 01:00:48,813
I order you to return!

1494
01:00:48,813 --> 01:00:50,448
- [Mike] Mach schnell!

1495
01:00:50,448 --> 01:00:51,982
- I am waiting for you.

1496
01:00:51,982 --> 01:00:53,383
(yelling)

1497
01:00:53,383 --> 01:00:54,218
- [Crow] I'm back
on catnip, man.

1498
01:00:54,218 --> 01:00:55,152
You gotta help me.

1499
01:00:55,152 --> 01:00:56,420
- Help me, Vadinho!

1500
01:00:56,420 --> 01:00:57,722
He's calling me.

1501
01:00:57,722 --> 01:00:58,823
Can you hear him,
can you hear him?

1502
01:00:58,823 --> 01:00:59,790
I can't fight it!

1503
01:00:59,790 --> 01:01:01,292
- Calm yourself!

1504
01:01:01,292 --> 01:01:03,227
- (yells) I can't,
I'm about to go!

1505
01:01:03,227 --> 01:01:04,595
- [Crow] Shoe in the scenery.

1506
01:01:04,595 --> 01:01:07,598
- If you do, you've
lost, he'll kill you.

1507
01:01:07,598 --> 01:01:08,933
You must resist.

1508
01:01:10,333 --> 01:01:14,172
Repeat with me, each man
is a god, each man is free.

1509
01:01:14,172 --> 01:01:17,608
Do not think of anything
else, concentrate!

1510
01:01:17,608 --> 01:01:19,543
Repeat, repeat with me.

1511
01:01:20,745 --> 01:01:23,413
Each man is a god,
each man is free.

1512
01:01:23,413 --> 01:01:25,383
Each man is a god.

1513
01:01:25,383 --> 01:01:26,650
- Each man is a god.

1514
01:01:26,650 --> 01:01:27,952
- Each man is free.

1515
01:01:27,952 --> 01:01:29,353
- Each man is free.

1516
01:01:29,353 --> 01:01:30,888
- Each man is a god.

1517
01:01:30,888 --> 01:01:32,223
- [Crow] Each man is a weenie.

1518
01:01:32,223 --> 01:01:33,623
- Each man is a god.

1519
01:01:33,623 --> 01:01:34,858
- [Vadinhoindho]
Each man is free.

1520
01:01:34,858 --> 01:01:36,127
- [Crow] Each man
is a puss, okay.

1521
01:01:36,127 --> 01:01:38,695
- [Tom] These walnuts are good.

1522
01:01:40,163 --> 01:01:43,367
- [Mike] Mr. Forbes is here
if you wanna go for a ride.

1523
01:01:43,367 --> 01:01:45,202
- I have taken away his powers.

1524
01:01:45,202 --> 01:01:46,670
- [Crow] So that's done anyway.

1525
01:01:46,670 --> 01:01:49,540
- And his will is broken,
but he's putting up

1526
01:01:49,540 --> 01:01:51,942
an unexpected resistance.

1527
01:01:51,942 --> 01:01:53,577
- I'll take care of it.

1528
01:01:53,577 --> 01:01:58,482
- Comb the area, find him,
but don't make any noise.

1529
01:01:58,482 --> 01:02:00,317
I don't want any
trouble around here.

1530
01:02:00,317 --> 01:02:05,088
- [Tom] If the police would
find out I'm pirating cable.

1531
01:02:05,088 --> 01:02:07,292
- [Mike] Break a few
more wills before lunch

1532
01:02:07,292 --> 01:02:09,793
then meet some death's
best on Fridays.

1533
01:02:09,793 --> 01:02:10,928
- Pumaman.

1534
01:02:10,928 --> 01:02:11,928
- [Tom] Pumaman!

1535
01:02:11,928 --> 01:02:14,365
- Pumaman, I am ordering you.

1536
01:02:15,533 --> 01:02:17,033
I am ordering you.

1537
01:02:18,602 --> 01:02:20,203
- [Crow] A fajita, is that okay?

1538
01:02:20,203 --> 01:02:21,972
- To kill yourself.

1539
01:02:21,972 --> 01:02:24,342
(dramatic music)

1540
01:02:24,342 --> 01:02:26,077
- [Mike] John Boy Walton.

1541
01:02:26,077 --> 01:02:27,478
- [Tom] I like the
other head better.

1542
01:02:27,478 --> 01:02:30,515
(dramatic music)

1543
01:02:30,515 --> 01:02:33,818
- It's all right
Vadinho, it's over.

1544
01:02:33,818 --> 01:02:35,218
- [Crow] Oh great,
so can we go, Mike?

1545
01:02:35,218 --> 01:02:36,887
- [Mike] No.

1546
01:02:36,887 --> 01:02:39,590
- Listen, I want you
to hear my epitaph.

1547
01:02:39,590 --> 01:02:41,358
- [Mike] I'm with stupid.

1548
01:02:41,358 --> 01:02:45,797
- He wasn't much in his life,
either as a man or a Pumaman,

1549
01:02:45,797 --> 01:02:47,698
and now he's worth
absolutely nothing.

1550
01:02:47,698 --> 01:02:48,900
- [Crow] The same as
when he was alive.

1551
01:02:48,900 --> 01:02:50,133
- It's not true.

1552
01:02:50,133 --> 01:02:52,337
You are a worthy man.

1553
01:02:52,337 --> 01:02:53,570
- [Tom] Worthy of a beating.

1554
01:02:53,570 --> 01:02:55,338
- You will be all right.

1555
01:02:55,338 --> 01:02:56,807
- Only if I lose a habit.

1556
01:02:56,807 --> 01:02:58,275
- Which one?

1557
01:02:58,275 --> 01:03:00,812
- [Crow] Nose picking,
public farting?

1558
01:03:00,812 --> 01:03:02,313
- Wanting to live!

1559
01:03:03,513 --> 01:03:05,583
- [Mike] Gotta clock
these windows quick.

1560
01:03:05,583 --> 01:03:07,050
(hand slapping)

1561
01:03:07,050 --> 01:03:09,787
- [Tom] C'mon, just let me
big a big, giant baby. (cries)

1562
01:03:09,787 --> 01:03:11,555
- No, let me go!

1563
01:03:11,555 --> 01:03:12,757
- [Crow] I just
wanna help you die

1564
01:03:12,757 --> 01:03:14,025
with a modicum of dignity.

1565
01:03:14,025 --> 01:03:15,993
- When you die, you
don't suffer anymore!

1566
01:03:15,993 --> 01:03:17,562
You don't have a master!

1567
01:03:17,562 --> 01:03:19,497
- You must not die, brother.

1568
01:03:19,497 --> 01:03:24,502
For you, or me, or Jane, for
all who want to live free.

1569
01:03:25,102 --> 01:03:25,770
Listen to me.

1570
01:03:25,770 --> 01:03:26,737
- [Mike] Whoa.

1571
01:03:26,737 --> 01:03:28,205
- Perhaps there is a way.

1572
01:03:28,205 --> 01:03:30,073
Only 10 minutes,
but you can do it.

1573
01:03:30,073 --> 01:03:34,012
Go to a deep sleep, 10
minutes with no life.

1574
01:03:34,012 --> 01:03:35,547
It is in your power.

1575
01:03:35,547 --> 01:03:38,115
- [Tom] I'm just sore is all.

1576
01:03:38,115 --> 01:03:40,283
- Kobras does not know it.

1577
01:03:41,218 --> 01:03:43,753
He cannot take it from you.

1578
01:03:43,753 --> 01:03:45,623
- [Crow] Please get off, I'm
feeling funny down there.

1579
01:03:45,623 --> 01:03:47,023
- Hold your breath.

1580
01:03:47,023 --> 01:03:50,027
Your heartbeat can slow down.

1581
01:03:50,027 --> 01:03:52,997
- [Mike] You just
have to not wiggle.

1582
01:03:52,997 --> 01:03:53,898
- Diminish.

1583
01:03:55,933 --> 01:03:57,268
- [Tom] I mean, anybody
would feel this right?

1584
01:03:57,268 --> 01:03:59,437
It's natural, right?

1585
01:03:59,437 --> 01:04:00,237
- Stop.

1586
01:04:02,072 --> 01:04:06,843
- [Crow] So pumas are suicidally
depressive mouth breathers?

1587
01:04:06,843 --> 01:04:10,280
- [Mike] We show you now the
general vicinity of the heart.

1588
01:04:10,280 --> 01:04:11,882
- That is right, Tony.

1589
01:04:11,882 --> 01:04:13,483
Let yourself go.

1590
01:04:13,483 --> 01:04:14,718
- [Tom] Stop working out.

1591
01:04:14,718 --> 01:04:16,787
- You are dead.

1592
01:04:16,787 --> 01:04:19,957
You are dead for
all, even for Kobras.

1593
01:04:22,593 --> 01:04:24,195
- [Crow] Duh, okay.

1594
01:04:25,997 --> 01:04:28,232
(Tom humming)

1595
01:04:28,232 --> 01:04:31,935
♪ Tink tink tink tinkle ♪

1596
01:04:31,935 --> 01:04:34,605
(door slamming)

1597
01:04:37,375 --> 01:04:40,110
(water dripping)

1598
01:04:44,882 --> 01:04:46,717
- Hey, look what we made, Mike.

1599
01:04:46,717 --> 01:04:49,287
- Why, that looks like, why
it looks for all the world

1600
01:04:49,287 --> 01:04:51,422
like a replica of the
head of Roger Whitaker.

1601
01:04:51,422 --> 01:04:53,523
- We made it with our
genuine Aztec mask.

1602
01:04:53,523 --> 01:04:55,158
- Wow, that's great.

1603
01:04:55,158 --> 01:04:56,493
I can hear him sing right now.

1604
01:04:56,493 --> 01:05:00,230
♪ I left my ship
out in the harbor ♪

1605
01:05:00,230 --> 01:05:02,900
I assume to gain control
of his mind and his will.

1606
01:05:02,900 --> 01:05:04,535
- There's no other reason
I can think of to own

1607
01:05:04,535 --> 01:05:07,037
a replica of the head of
Roger Whitaker. (chuckles)

1608
01:05:07,037 --> 01:05:09,740
- Yeah exactly, but I have to
ask why, why Roger Whitaker?

1609
01:05:09,740 --> 01:05:11,175
Why not say, Barbara--

1610
01:05:11,175 --> 01:05:13,210
- Feldon, right we thought
of that, okay Mike?

1611
01:05:13,210 --> 01:05:15,913
And Sting, and Chipmunk,
and Senator John Warner.

1612
01:05:15,913 --> 01:05:18,415
- And Puff Daddy, and Al
Checky, and Web Pierce,

1613
01:05:18,415 --> 01:05:20,450
and Judy Carne, and
Joan Sutherland.

1614
01:05:20,450 --> 01:05:21,918
- And George Lindsay,
and Barbara Bush--

1615
01:05:21,918 --> 01:05:23,787
- And people like that, and
Mike, when you only have time

1616
01:05:23,787 --> 01:05:25,488
to effectively
control one person--

1617
01:05:25,488 --> 01:05:26,890
- We have other
things to do, Mike.

1618
01:05:26,890 --> 01:05:28,625
- Then Roger Whitaker
is the perfect choice.

1619
01:05:28,625 --> 01:05:30,160
Take our word for it.

1620
01:05:30,160 --> 01:05:32,663
It's who we got, now what
do you wanna do with him?

1621
01:05:32,663 --> 01:05:35,933
- Well, I can' think
of anything at all.

1622
01:05:35,933 --> 01:05:39,770
- Use your imagination,
man, it's Roger Whitaker.

1623
01:05:39,770 --> 01:05:41,538
I mean, that means songs, sure,

1624
01:05:41,538 --> 01:05:42,807
but he can probably
do other things,

1625
01:05:42,807 --> 01:05:44,575
light typing and filing.

1626
01:05:44,575 --> 01:05:46,243
Maybe you need help
with your hand washing.

1627
01:05:46,243 --> 01:05:47,412
- No, no I don't.

1628
01:05:47,412 --> 01:05:49,280
Frankly, I think
it's a waste of time.

1629
01:05:49,280 --> 01:05:50,882
- Oh fine, we go to
all this trouble,

1630
01:05:50,882 --> 01:05:53,617
hand Mike Roger Whitaker,
and he drops the ball.

1631
01:05:53,617 --> 01:05:55,552
- Here's the wheel,
here's the Mike.

1632
01:05:55,552 --> 01:05:58,288
(mumbling) What do I
do with this? (mumbles)

1633
01:05:58,288 --> 01:06:00,590
Now you can just go on with
your Roger Whitaker free life,

1634
01:06:00,590 --> 01:06:02,793
you poor sap, but the
next time you need to hear

1635
01:06:02,793 --> 01:06:05,162
"Durham Town," you're
on your own, good luck.

1636
01:06:05,162 --> 01:06:06,897
- Remember though, we
control Roger Whitaker.

1637
01:06:06,897 --> 01:06:07,898
- That's right.

1638
01:06:07,898 --> 01:06:09,133
- So watch your back!

1639
01:06:09,133 --> 01:06:10,400
Roger Whitaker could be
on you at any moment.

1640
01:06:10,400 --> 01:06:11,402
- There he is!

1641
01:06:11,402 --> 01:06:12,403
- Whoa!

1642
01:06:12,403 --> 01:06:13,937
- I'm kidding, this time.

1643
01:06:13,937 --> 01:06:15,405
- Yeah, look at him run.

1644
01:06:15,405 --> 01:06:16,907
We'll be right back everybody.

1645
01:06:16,907 --> 01:06:21,078
In the meantime, be on the
lookout for Roger Whitaker.

1646
01:06:21,078 --> 01:06:23,413
(chuckling)

1647
01:06:25,683 --> 01:06:28,252
(upbeat music)

1648
01:06:32,523 --> 01:06:35,358
- [Tom] There he
is, Roger Whitaker.

1649
01:06:35,358 --> 01:06:37,060
- [Mike] I'm scared.

1650
01:06:37,060 --> 01:06:40,063
Oh, I overdid it
on the Fancy Feast.

1651
01:06:42,533 --> 01:06:43,967
- [Tom] Later, Mob
Barker and the gang

1652
01:06:43,967 --> 01:06:45,903
come to finish him off.

1653
01:06:47,137 --> 01:06:49,307
- [Mike] Tee hee, tee hee.

1654
01:06:50,708 --> 01:06:55,245
- [Tom] They're here and the
cupcakes are still in the oven.

1655
01:06:56,447 --> 01:06:59,417
- [Crow] Friends are
visiting for murder.

1656
01:07:02,052 --> 01:07:03,453
- [Mike] Pumaman.

1657
01:07:06,990 --> 01:07:10,160
- [Tom] It's Cliff
Claven, hey Cliffy.

1658
01:07:11,762 --> 01:07:13,463
- [Crow] So let's cut
his ears and paws off.

1659
01:07:13,463 --> 01:07:15,632
We get the 50 buck bounty.

1660
01:07:16,633 --> 01:07:19,035
- [Mike] So tense right here.

1661
01:07:25,843 --> 01:07:28,445
- [Crow] Tell Santa I love him.

1662
01:07:33,383 --> 01:07:36,420
- [Mike] You won't
get my monte auto.

1663
01:07:37,287 --> 01:07:38,555
- He's had it.

1664
01:07:38,555 --> 01:07:42,660
- [Crow] Chickenpox, he
won't catch it from us.

1665
01:07:42,660 --> 01:07:44,662
- [Tom] So anyway, do
you have it in loading?

1666
01:07:44,662 --> 01:07:47,698
- We found him, he's
committed suicide.

1667
01:07:47,698 --> 01:07:49,833
Should I put a bullet
in him just to be sure?

1668
01:07:49,833 --> 01:07:51,602
- [Mike] No, that
would be cheating.

1669
01:07:51,602 --> 01:07:55,072
- No, it has to look like
an unfortunate accident,

1670
01:07:55,072 --> 01:07:57,307
but be sure that he's dead.

1671
01:07:58,208 --> 01:07:59,710
- You can count on it, sir.

1672
01:07:59,710 --> 01:08:01,312
- [Crow] Boss says I'm in charge
and I get your lunch today

1673
01:08:01,312 --> 01:08:02,480
and you drive.

1674
01:08:04,548 --> 01:08:06,917
- [Tom] Can't you
just accept it, Tom?

1675
01:08:06,917 --> 01:08:10,788
- [Mike] I don't know,
I just don't know.

1676
01:08:10,788 --> 01:08:13,290
- [Crow] Why do I have
to stay in the car?

1677
01:08:13,290 --> 01:08:15,993
- You couldn't find a corpse
more dead than this one.

1678
01:08:15,993 --> 01:08:17,662
- What are you gonna
do with the body?

1679
01:08:17,662 --> 01:08:19,597
- Leave him like he is.

1680
01:08:24,067 --> 01:08:25,903
- [Tom] Are they gone?

1681
01:08:30,173 --> 01:08:32,910
- [Crow] I have
slacks like that.

1682
01:08:34,312 --> 01:08:35,578
- [Mike] No, see this was
just really avoidable.

1683
01:08:35,578 --> 01:08:38,348
(dramatic music)

1684
01:08:40,150 --> 01:08:41,218
- [Tom] I was
alive for a second.

1685
01:08:41,218 --> 01:08:43,187
Now I'm dead again, go away.

1686
01:08:43,187 --> 01:08:45,322
- Why don't you shoot him?

1687
01:08:45,322 --> 01:08:46,823
- Because Kobras said not to.

1688
01:08:46,823 --> 01:08:50,160
- [Crow] You are so
Kobras whipped, man.

1689
01:08:52,395 --> 01:08:53,697
- [Mike] I'm just thinking
about the last dead guy

1690
01:08:53,697 --> 01:08:56,867
who sprang up and
killed half our men.

1691
01:08:58,635 --> 01:09:00,037
- [Tom] It seems I have
you in a bit of a bind,

1692
01:09:00,037 --> 01:09:04,073
don't I Mr. Dead
Human? (buzzing)

1693
01:09:04,073 --> 01:09:09,078
- [Crow] Hate to see you
sneeze right now. (buzzing)

1694
01:09:10,780 --> 01:09:12,282
- [Tom] Here's the deal.

1695
01:09:12,282 --> 01:09:13,550
I don't make you sneeze
and you give me your Pope

1696
01:09:13,550 --> 01:09:14,818
for the rest of your life.

1697
01:09:14,818 --> 01:09:17,555
(dramatic music)

1698
01:09:19,290 --> 01:09:21,692
- [Mike] Even when dead,
his hair looks terrific.

1699
01:09:21,692 --> 01:09:24,462
(dramatic music)

1700
01:09:26,197 --> 01:09:28,298
- [Crow] I just have a really
hard time making decisions,

1701
01:09:28,298 --> 01:09:30,633
you know, you guys?

1702
01:09:30,633 --> 01:09:33,370
(engine revving)

1703
01:09:35,105 --> 01:09:36,540
- [Mike] Pumaman.

1704
01:09:39,943 --> 01:09:42,078
- [Crow] No, I feel good
about our decision, I do.

1705
01:09:42,078 --> 01:09:44,748
No, let's go back, no forget it.

1706
01:09:46,517 --> 01:09:50,320
- [Tom] Certainly, this
is a victory for good.

1707
01:09:52,657 --> 01:09:55,358
- You succeeded, they
think you're dead,

1708
01:09:55,358 --> 01:09:57,393
and now they will
leave you alone.

1709
01:09:57,393 --> 01:09:59,630
- [Mike] To be left alone,
the goal of every great hero.

1710
01:09:59,630 --> 01:10:02,733
- Yeah, but what about the mask?

1711
01:10:02,733 --> 01:10:05,035
- Forget it, you
are only a man now.

1712
01:10:05,035 --> 01:10:07,103
You cannot do it.

1713
01:10:07,103 --> 01:10:08,305
- [Crow] Did I say man?

1714
01:10:08,305 --> 01:10:11,775
You're not a man, more
like a box turtle.

1715
01:10:11,775 --> 01:10:14,043
I'm getting out of here.

1716
01:10:14,043 --> 01:10:16,880
- [Tom] Do I get
to keep the cape?

1717
01:10:19,650 --> 01:10:24,322
- [Mike] I'm finally gonna
get my pennies counted anyway.

1718
01:10:24,322 --> 01:10:27,090
- And that dynamite's
for that bastard, Kobras?

1719
01:10:27,090 --> 01:10:28,658
- I said forget it.

1720
01:10:28,658 --> 01:10:30,460
- And should I also forget Jane,

1721
01:10:30,460 --> 01:10:32,462
and the fact that Kobras
wants to take over the world?

1722
01:10:32,462 --> 01:10:34,030
- [Crow] Am I supposed
to forget Jane?

1723
01:10:34,030 --> 01:10:35,598
- The gods have abandoned us,

1724
01:10:35,598 --> 01:10:38,268
or perhaps they want sacrifice.

1725
01:10:38,268 --> 01:10:39,537
- What sacrifice?

1726
01:10:39,537 --> 01:10:40,337
- My life.

1727
01:10:41,772 --> 01:10:44,708
- You wanna destroy Kobras
with a suicide action?

1728
01:10:44,708 --> 01:10:46,543
There's got to be another way.

